# This repo is developed on Windows with core.autocrlf=true, so git rewrites line
# endings on checkout. For binary files that would corrupt the file. Git's automatic
# binary detection usually catches it, but it is a heuristic (it samples the first
# few KB for NUL bytes) — these rules make it explicit rather than lucky.
#
# Symptom if this is ever removed: `git add` warns "LF will be replaced by CRLF"
# on a binary path, and clones get a corrupted file that the original machine
# still reads fine.

*.pdf  binary
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.ico  binary
*.webp binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf  binary
*.otf  binary
*.eot  binary
*.zip  binary
*.gz   binary
*.docx binary
*.xlsx binary
*.pptx binary
